hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1689","Narrated to us ‘Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ghāfiqī: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb: On the authority of Dāwūd ibn Qays: On the authority of ‘Abdullāh ibn Suwayd al-Anṣārī: On the authority of his paternal aunt, the wife of Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī (may Allah be pleased with her), who said:\n\n> “O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), I love to pray with you.”\n\nHe (ﷺ) said:\n\n> “I know that you love to pray with me. But your prayer in your private chamber (ḥujrah) is better than your prayer in your house. Your prayer in your house is better than your prayer in the mosque of your people. And your prayer in the mosque of your people is better than your prayer in my mosque.”\n\nSo she ordered, and a mosque was built for her in the farthest and darkest part of her house, where she would pray until she met Allah, the Almighty and Majestic.”\n\nCHAPTER:"
